      "observed": "U9 74LVC1G86 is present; pin1 connects to U1 GPIO9, pin2 connects to U2 T-/J1 pin1, and pin4 connects to U3 pin8 (NC).",
      "expected": "No U9; U2 T- should connect only to J1 pin1 and U2 pin2; U3 pin8 should be unconnected as stated in the spec.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"34\") (name \"Net-(U9-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"23\") (pinfunction \"GPIO9\") ...) (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"1\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"35\") (name \"Net-(U9-Pad2)\") ... (node (ref \"J1\") (pin \"1\") ...) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"T-\") ...) (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"2\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"36\") (name \"Net-(U9-Pad4)\") ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"NC\") ...) (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"4\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Pin 8 (NC) is left unconnected on all three parts (confirmed: unconnected-(U2/U3/U4-NC-Pad8) nets in controller.net)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "whose two pins wire directly to the MAX31855's differential thermocouple inputs T+ (pin 3) and T- (pin 2)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "U9 loads the U2 thermocouple T- input and GPIO9 strapping pin, and violates the specified no-connect on U3 pin8; this can disturb thermocouple measurements and adds an unplanned active component.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain an extra 74LVC1G86 (U9) that is not in the specification; it loads U2's thermocouple T- input and connects to U3's NC pin, contradicting the spec's statement that all MAX31855 NC pins are unconnected."
}

